      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182164/assets/468fd25032d1a36e1658331053a33652cef7ff9ce3d9c95b729d6a7b7ebf1672.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the length of $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is $5d+12,$ and $AB=3d+2.$ If $C$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{BD},$ find the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that according to the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BD,\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =AD-AB \\\\  & =(5d+12)-(3d+2) \\\\  & =2d+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $C$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{BD},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =AB+\\frac{1}{2}BD \\\\  & =3d+2+\\frac{1}{2}(2d+10) \\\\  & =3d+2+d+5 \\\\  & =4d+7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
